     The ttoolloowweerr() and ttoolloowweerr__ll() functions convert an upper-case letter to
     the corresponding lower-case letter.  The argument must be representable
     as an _u_n_s_i_g_n_e_d _c_h_a_r or the value of EOF.

     The ttoolloowweerr__ll() function takes an explicit locale argument, whereas the
     ttoolloowweerr() function uses the current global or per-thread locale.

